son by Bathsheba, i.e., the first after their legal marriage (2 Sam. 12). He was probably born about B.C. 1035 (1 Chr. 22:5; 29:1).","verses":273,"father":"David","mother":"Bathsheba","v":[1,2,6]},{"id":"israel_682","name":"Israel","also":"","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[2,10]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[10]},{"id":"asaph_330","name":"Asaph","also":"","summary":"A Levite; one of the leaders of David’s choir (1 Chr. 6:39). Psalms 50 and 73-83 inclusive are attributed to him. He is mentioned along with David as skilled in music, and a “seer” (2 Chr. 29:30).","verses":32,"father":"Berechiah","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"jeduthun_1224","name":"Jeduthun","also":"Ethan","summary":"A Levite of the family of Merari, one of the leaders of the temple music (1 Chr. 6:44; 15:17, 19). He was probably the same as Jeduthun.","verses":13,"father":"Kishi","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"heman_1490","name":"Heman","also":"","summary":"Grandson of Samuel (1 Chr. 6:33; 15:17), to whom the 88th Psalm probably was inscribed.","verses":12,"father":"Joel","mother":"","v":[12]}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[2]},{"id":"zion_1263","name":"Zion","kind":"Mountain","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Sunny; height, one of the eminences on which Jerusalem was built. It was surrounded on all sides, except the north, by deep valleys, that of the Tyropoeon separating it from Moriah, which it surpasses in height by 105 feet.","verses":140,"v":[2]},{"id":"most_holy_place_827","name":"most holy place","kind":"","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"One of the two portions into which the tabernacle was divided (Ex. 26:31; 37:17-25; Heb. 9:2). It was 20 cubits long and 10 in height and breadth.","verses":12,"v":[7]},{"id":"holy_place_575","name":"Holy Place","kind":"","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"One of the two portions into which the tabernacle was divided (Ex. 26:31; 37:17-25; Heb. 9:2). It was 20 cubits long and 10 in height and breadth.","verses":14,"v":[9,11]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[10]},{"id":"horeb_576","name":"Horeb","kind":"Church","lat":28.58771,"lon":33.92168,"summary":"Desert or mountain of the dried-up ground, a general name for the whole mountain range of which Sinai was one of the summits (Ex. 3:1; 17:6; 33:6; Ps. 106:19, etc.).","verses":16,"v":[10]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3605,3605,4399,4399,834,8010,6213,6213,1004,1004,1004,3068,3068,3068,7999,7999,8010,8010,935,935,935,935,1,1,1732,6944,6944,3701,2091,2091,3605,3605,3627,3627,5414,5414,5414,214,214,214,1004,1004,1004,430,430],[227,227,227,8010,6950,413,3389,2205,2205,3478,3478,4294,4294,7218,1,1,1,3478,3478,3478,5927,5927,727,727,1285,1285,1285,3068,3068,3068,6726,6726,5892,5892,1732,1732],[3605,3605,376,376,3478,3478,6950,6950,4428,4428,4428,2282,2282,2282,7637,7637,7637,2320],[3605,3605,2205,2205,3478,3478,935,935,3881,3881,5375,5375,727,727],[5927,5927,5927,5927,727,727,853,168,168,4150,4150,853,3605,168,6944,3627,3881,3881,3548,5927,592